<Project>

  <!--
    Host context registry.

    A hosting context is a front door: the way a caller arrives at "run this
    command with these arguments". adr/proposed/FluentMigrator-Host-Design.md
    enumerates eight of them, all resolving to the same IMigrationCommand set
    through MigrationHost — a CLI parses argv, MSBuild hands over task
    properties, Aspire hands over a command payload, MCP hands over a tool
    call. The framework difference between them is an adapter; the difference
    *here* is one property.

      <HostContexts>dotnet-cli;aspire</HostContexts>

    Selection is a ';'-separated property rather than an item list for the
    same reason $(SourceModelConvention) is: MSBuild evaluates all properties
    before any item, so only a property can gate the imports below — and
    gating imports is what lets a pack contribute its own PackageReference
    instead of the SDK hardcoding one per front door.

    Each pack under hosts/ contributes exactly one HostContextDefinition:

      Package        the adapter package implementing this front door
      ReferenceKind  package  - referenced by the host project
                     tool     - invoked out of process (dotnet tool), never referenced
      Invocation     how the caller supplies the command and its arguments
      Availability   shipping - the package exists today
                     planned  - described by the Host ADR, not yet shipped;
                                selecting it is legal and recorded in the
                                manifest, it simply adds no reference
      Discovery      true when the context renders MigrationHost.Discover()
                     metadata rather than hardcoding a command list
      Version        resolved from that pack's version property, if set

    Extension is declaring another pack, never teaching the SDK about a new
    front door: point $(CustomHostContextPacks) (a ';'-separated list of
    props file paths) at your own.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <HostContexts Condition="'$(HostContexts)' == ''">dotnet-cli</HostContexts>

    <!-- Delimited on both ends so a pack can test for ';name;' and not
         match a context whose name merely contains its own. -->
    <_HostContextSelection>;$(HostContexts);</_HostContextSelection>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)hosts/*.props" />
  <Import Project="$(CustomHostContextPacks)" Condition="'$(CustomHostContextPacks)' != ''" />

  <ItemGroup>
    <HostContext Include="$(HostContexts)" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
